      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0RsFtb0ATXtGL5fGWmNpn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -271.9482096522304,
      "y": 56136.634734024046,
      "width": 759,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b66",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2029078091,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 1502729061,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790749997071,
      "created": 1790749969465,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Next Question — Service Layer\nImagine we have two different APIs:\nPOST /projects/10/tasks/\nPOST /bulk-import/tasks/\n\nBoth need the exact same business rules for creating a task.\nWhere should we put the common task-creation logic?\n\nA) Duplicate it in both APIViews\nB) Put it in TaskService.create_task() and call the service from both\nC) Put everything in the serializer\nD) Put everything in the frontend\nWhat's your answer?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Next Question — Service Layer\nImagine we have two different APIs:\nPOST /projects/10/tasks/\nPOST /bulk-import/tasks/\n\nBoth need the exact same business rules for creating a task.\nWhere should we put the common task-creation logic?\n\nA) Duplicate it in both APIViews\nB) Put it in TaskService.create_task() and call the service from both\nC) Put everything in the serializer\nD) Put everything in the frontend\nWhat's your answer?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "j0qMgajiKunkD_eb3PC5A",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -195.3271159022304,
      "y": 56493.263640274046,
      "width": 704,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b67",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1399648645,
      "version": 37,
      "versionNonce": 893927371,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750147794,
      "created": 1790750051734,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ Correct — B\nThis is one of the main reasons we use a Service Layer.\nInstead of duplicating the same business logic:\n\nAPI 1 ──────┐\n            ├──→ TaskService.create_task()\nAPI 2 ──────┘\n\nBoth APIs can reuse the same workflow.\n\nOne important concept: Service ≠ Database wrapper\nDon't think:\n\"Service layer is just where I put Task.objects.create().\"\n\nThe real purpose is to represent a business operation.\n\nFor example:\nTaskService.create_task(...)\nTaskService.complete_task(...)\nTaskService.assign_task(...)\nTaskService.move_task(...)\n\nThese methods can coordinate multiple models and business rules.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ Correct — B\nThis is one of the main reasons we use a Service Layer.\nInstead of duplicating the same business logic:\n\nAPI 1 ──────┐\n            ├──→ TaskService.create_task()\nAPI 2 ──────┘\n\nBoth APIs can reuse the same workflow.\n\nOne important concept: Service ≠ Database wrapper\nDon't think:\n\"Service layer is just where I put Task.objects.create().\"\n\nThe real purpose is to represent a business operation.\n\nFor example:\nTaskService.create_task(...)\nTaskService.complete_task(...)\nTaskService.assign_task(...)\nTaskService.move_task(...)\n\nThese methods can coordinate multiple models and business rules.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nMUtl16UbXI3ues6uTmSa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -225.4677409022304,
      "y": 56942.517546524046,
      "width": 704,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b68",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 485922699,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1217949899,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750100533,
      "created": 1790750099629,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "These methods can coordinate multiple models and business rules.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "These methods can coordinate multiple models and business rules.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hEQzIQmhJ8stL0kYmb4gi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -289.0732096522304,
      "y": 57169.134734024046,
      "width": 748,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b69",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1568518059,
      "version": 11,
      "versionNonce": 1182435973,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750176225,
      "created": 1790750164401,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Final Service Layer question\nSuppose TaskService.create_task() does this:\n1. Create Task\n2. Create ActivityLog\n3. Update Project statistics\n\nShould we use transaction.atomic() around these database operations?\nA) Yes, when these changes need to succeed or fail together\nB) No, transaction.atomic() is only for SELECT queries\nC) No, transactions are only needed for authentication\nD) Only the frontend needs transactions",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Final Service Layer question\nSuppose TaskService.create_task() does this:\n1. Create Task\n2. Create ActivityLog\n3. Update Project statistics\n\nShould we use transaction.atomic() around these database operations?\nA) Yes, when these changes need to succeed or fail together\nB) No, transaction.atomic() is only for SELECT queries\nC) No, transactions are only needed for authentication\nD) Only the frontend needs transactions",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vwKLQsY81i1koxvrbtxWg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -211.9364909022304,
      "y": 57468.912077774046,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 1400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6A",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1198488741,
      "version": 24,
      "versionNonce": 1198935691,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750293087,
      "created": 1790750202369,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ Correct — A\nExactly.\nIf these operations represent one logical business operation and we\ndon't want partial updates, we use a transaction:\n\nTask creation\n     ↓\nActivity Log\n     ↓\nProject statistics\n     ↓\n ┌─────────────────┐\n │ All succeed ✅  │\n │     → COMMIT    │\n └─────────────────┘\n\nIf one fails ❌\n     ↓\nROLLBACK\n\nfrom django.db import transaction\n\nclass TaskService:\n\n    @staticmethod\n    @transaction.atomic\n    def create_task(*, user, project, validated_data):\n\n        task = Task.objects.create(\n            project=project,\n            created_by=user,\n            **validated_data\n        )\n\n        ActivityLog.objects.create(\n            task=task,\n            user=user,\n            action=\"TASK_CREATED\"\n        )\n\n        project.task_count += 1\n        project.save(update_fields=[\"task_count\"])\n\n        return task\n\nOne important nuance\nWe don't automatically put every database operation inside a\ntransaction.\nFor example, a simple:\n\n\nProject.objects.get(id=10)\n\ndoesn't normally need its own explicit transaction.\nUse a transaction when multiple changes need to maintain a consistent\nstate.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ Correct — A\nExactly.\nIf these operations represent one logical business operation and we don't want partial updates, we use a transaction:\n\nTask creation\n     ↓\nActivity Log\n     ↓\nProject statistics\n     ↓\n ┌─────────────────┐\n │ All succeed ✅  │\n │     → COMMIT    │\n └─────────────────┘\n\nIf one fails ❌\n     ↓\nROLLBACK\n\nfrom django.db import transaction\n\nclass TaskService:\n\n    @staticmethod\n    @transaction.atomic\n    def create_task(*, user, project, validated_data):\n\n        task = Task.objects.create(\n            project=project,\n            created_by=user,\n            **validated_data\n        )\n\n        ActivityLog.objects.create(\n            task=task,\n            user=user,\n            action=\"TASK_CREATED\"\n        )\n\n        project.task_count += 1\n        project.save(update_fields=[\"task_count\"])\n\n        return task\n\nOne important nuance\nWe don't automatically put every database operation inside a transaction.\nFor example, a simple:\n\n\nProject.objects.get(id=10)\n\ndoesn't normally need its own explicit transaction.\nUse a transaction when multiple changes need to maintain a consistent state.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "x2aOJ4IyUL9r7sNpLQxNy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -283.8114909022304,
      "y": 58915.404265274046,
      "width": 187,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6B",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2138569157,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 313799653,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750324496,
      "created": 1790750322250,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "responsibilities:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "responsibilities:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8SmON9dgdKQLTja8rMcbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -231.8114909022304,
      "y": 58953.404265274046,
      "width": 308,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1969859787,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1478114475,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750329979,
      "created": 1790750328383,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "APIView\n→ HTTP\n\nPermission\n→ Authorization\n\nSerializer\n→ Validation / Serialization\n\nService\n→ Business workflow\n\nTransaction\n→ Atomic database changes\n\nORM\n→ Database interaction",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "APIView\n→ HTTP\n\nPermission\n→ Authorization\n\nSerializer\n→ Validation / Serialization\n\nService\n→ Business workflow\n\nTransaction\n→ Atomic database changes\n\nORM\n→ Database interaction",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "aSZhLggvTB4RNRYwvzP-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -284.9364909022304,
      "y": 59510.279265274046,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 991267237,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 1276406699,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750369999,
      "created": 1790750340417,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Next topic: Pagination & Filtering\nWe'll learn how this:\nGET /projects/\n\nshould work when your organization has 100,000 projects, instead of\nreturning everything at once.\n\nWe'll cover:\n- Pagination\n- Limit/offset\n- Cursor pagination\n- Filtering\n- Searching\n- Sorting\n- Database implications\n- How to design production APIs\nThen we'll apply it to our Enterprise Workspace.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Next topic: Pagination & Filtering\nWe'll learn how this:\nGET /projects/\n\nshould work when your organization has 100,000 projects, instead of returning everything at once.\n\nWe'll cover:\n- Pagination\n- Limit/offset\n- Cursor pagination\n- Filtering\n- Searching\n- Sorting\n- Database implications\n- How to design production APIs\nThen we'll apply it to our Enterprise Workspace.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tHt-qhnDCFC1WNRCNjUR4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -230.2138346522304,
      "y": 59970.017546524046,
      "width": 1022.53125,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6E",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2068344683,
      "version": 140,
      "versionNonce": 739753227,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750671152,
      "created": 1790750557002,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is an important backend topic because APIs that work fine with 100 records can become\nproblematic with millions.\n\n1. The basic problem\nImagine our API:\nGET /projects/\n\nToday we have: 100 projects\n\nWe could return: {\n  \"projects\": [\n    {...},\n    {...},\n    {...}\n  ]\n}\n\nBut imagine an organization has:\n\n1,000,000 projects\n\nIf we do: Project.objects.all()\n\nand return everything, we potentially have to:\nDatabase\n   ↓\n1,000,000 rows\n   ↓\nDjango\n   ↓\nSerialize 1,000,000 objects\n   ↓\nHuge HTTP response\n   ↓\nClient\n\nThat's inefficient.\nWe instead want:\n\nGET /projects/?page=1&page_size=20\nand return only 20 projects.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is an important backend topic because APIs that work fine with 100 records can become  problematic with millions.\n\n1. The basic problem\nImagine our API:\nGET /projects/\n\nToday we have: 100 projects\n\nWe could return: {\n  \"projects\": [\n    {...},\n    {...},\n    {...}\n  ]\n}\n\nBut imagine an organization has:\n\n1,000,000 projects\n\nIf we do: Project.objects.all()\n\nand return everything, we potentially have to:\nDatabase\n   ↓\n1,000,000 rows\n   ↓\nDjango\n   ↓\nSerialize 1,000,000 objects\n   ↓\nHuge HTTP response\n   ↓\nClient\n\nThat's inefficient.\nWe instead want:\n\nGET /projects/?page=1&page_size=20\nand return only 20 projects.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ubk50caX5mgQsOtsQVByM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -292.8114909022304,
      "y": 61051.404265274046,
      "width": 242,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1608987883,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1052195019,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750680251,
      "created": 1790750678687,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. What is Pagination?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. What is Pagination?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "egMq1UpD6g3YmMCvjMpGQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -243.8114909022304,
      "y": 61082.279265274046,
      "width": 704,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1978870661,
      "version": 16,
      "versionNonce": 250859333,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750708135,
      "created": 1790750686119,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Pagination means dividing a large result set into smaller pages.\nFor example:\n\n100 projects\n\nPage 1 → Projects 1-20\nPage 2 → Projects 21-40\nPage 3 → Projects 41-60\nPage 4 → Projects 61-80\nPage 5 → Projects 81-100\n\nThe client doesn't receive all 100 at once.\nA typical response might look like:\n\n{\n    \"count\": 100,\n    \"next\": \"/projects/?page=2\",\n    \"previous\": null,\n    \"results\": [\n        {...},\n        {...}\n    ]\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Pagination means dividing a large result set into smaller pages.\nFor example:\n\n100 projects\n\nPage 1 → Projects 1-20\nPage 2 → Projects 21-40\nPage 3 → Projects 41-60\nPage 4 → Projects 61-80\nPage 5 → Projects 81-100\n\nThe client doesn't receive all 100 at once.\nA typical response might look like:\n\n{\n    \"count\": 100,\n    \"next\": \"/projects/?page=2\",\n    \"previous\": null,\n    \"results\": [\n        {...},\n        {...}\n    ]\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7-pnXYf3m32mRdRSu21UZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -297.8114909022304,
      "y": 61705.404265274046,
      "width": 341,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1630402917,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1584584581,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750739901,
      "created": 1790750737786,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Why is pagination important?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Why is pagination important?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "I6pQkU3L5ygoONt__fYdS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -227.9325846522304,
      "y": 61745.162077774046,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 623488811,
      "version": 29,
      "versionNonce": 1359943307,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750807123,
      "created": 1790750746104,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "There are several reasons.\nMemory\nWithout pagination:\n\n1 million rows\n      ↓\nDjango memory ↑\n\nWith pagination:\n20 rows\n      ↓\nMuch smaller processing\n\n\nNetwork\nSending 1 million objects over HTTP is obviously expensive.\nPagination reduces the response size.\n\n\nResponse time\nThe database and application don't have to process the entire result set\nfor every request.\n\nUser experience\nA UI can display:\n\nProjects 1–20\n[Next →]\n\ninstead of waiting for a gigantic response.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "There are several reasons.\nMemory\nWithout pagination:\n\n1 million rows\n      ↓\nDjango memory ↑\n\nWith pagination:\n20 rows\n      ↓\nMuch smaller processing\n\n\nNetwork\nSending 1 million objects over HTTP is obviously expensive.\nPagination reduces the response size.\n\n\nResponse time\nThe database and application don't have to process the entire result set for every request.\n\nUser experience\nA UI can display:\n\nProjects 1–20\n[Next →]\n\ninstead of waiting for a gigantic response.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "flsCNErQzf7xT03u52UHI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -288.8114909022304,
      "y": 62560.283171524046,
      "width": 517,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 769326699,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 129856075,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750814401,
      "created": 1790750812837,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Limit / Offset\nOne common pagination approach is limit/offset.\nFor example:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4. Limit / Offset\nOne common pagination approach is limit/offset.\nFor example:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "W_yPvuKmC2ohniZxOd_Nc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -244.9403971522304,
      "y": 62650.521452774046,
      "width": 407.3125,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 180214277,
      "version": 34,
      "versionNonce": 903249733,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750887822,
      "created": 1790750820666,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GET /projects/?limit=20&offset=0\nmeans:\n\nGive me 20 projects\nstarting from position 0\n\nNext:\n\nGET /projects/?limit=20&offset=20\nmeans:\nSkip first 20\nGive me next 20\n\nConceptually:\n\nProjects:\n\n0 ────────────────────────────────\n  1  2  3 ... 20\n                ↑\n              limit=20\n\n20 ───────────────────────────────\n   21 22 23 ... 40\n\nThis is simple and commonly used.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GET /projects/?limit=20&offset=0\nmeans:\n\nGive me 20 projects\nstarting from position 0\n\nNext:\n\nGET /projects/?limit=20&offset=20\nmeans:\nSkip first 20\nGive me next 20\n\nConceptually:\n\nProjects:\n\n0 ────────────────────────────────\n  1  2  3 ... 20\n                ↑\n              limit=20\n\n20 ───────────────────────────────\n   21 22 23 ... 40\n\nThis is simple and commonly used.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IPC5iEDCSXOzqlBut8NRO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -316.8114909022304,
      "y": 63363.783171524046,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1087285605,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 126977925,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750895419,
      "created": 1790750893784,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5. But there's a problem with Offset",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5. But there's a problem with Offset",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "qoUbJZlYcj-SHYBVu1P2G",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -260.9325846522304,
      "y": 63401.513640274046,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1596981035,
      "version": 16,
      "versionNonce": 606658757,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750938515,
      "created": 1790750903621,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Suppose we have:\nProject 1\nProject 2\nProject 3\n...\nProject 1000000\n\nYou request: ?limit=20&offset=900000\n\nThe database may need to work through a large number of rows before\nreaching that offset, depending on the query and execution plan.\nSo for very large datasets, offset pagination can become less\nattractive.\nThis is where cursor pagination becomes important.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Suppose we have:\nProject 1\nProject 2\nProject 3\n...\nProject 1000000\n\nYou request: ?limit=20&offset=900000\n\nThe database may need to work through a large number of rows before reaching that offset, depending on the query and execution plan.\nSo for very large datasets, offset pagination can become less attractive.\nThis is where cursor pagination becomes important.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "S4Y713MnIWA8FQQ5pvMzw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -312.8114909022304,
      "y": 63806.013640274046,
      "width": 220,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 379222757,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1812777221,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790750946519,
      "created": 1790750945088,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. Cursor Pagination\nInstead of saying:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. Cursor Pagination\nInstead of saying:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZRiE4-0x8MqGpEpwCy-qC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -271.8153971522304,
      "y": 63859.009734024046,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 902636971,
      "version": 28,
      "versionNonce": 2122368997,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751008182,
      "created": 1790750950836,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Skip 900,000 records.\"\nwe say:\n\"Give me the next 20 records after this particular position.\"\n\nExample:\nGET /projects/?cursor=abc123\n\nThe cursor represents a position in the ordered result set.\nConceptually:\n\nProject 1\nProject 2\nProject 3\n...\nProject 500\n      ↑\n    cursor\n      ↓\nProject 501\nProject 502\n...\n\nThe next request says:\nContinue from here.\n\nCursor pagination is particularly useful for large or frequently\nchanging datasets.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Skip 900,000 records.\"\nwe say:\n\"Give me the next 20 records after this particular position.\"\n\nExample:\nGET /projects/?cursor=abc123\n\nThe cursor represents a position in the ordered result set.\nConceptually:\n\nProject 1\nProject 2\nProject 3\n...\nProject 500\n      ↑\n    cursor\n      ↓\nProject 501\nProject 502\n...\n\nThe next request says:\nContinue from here.\n\nCursor pagination is particularly useful for large or frequently changing datasets.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "WhUqkPDKsoQ2D8NaPRFqJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -345.8114909022304,
      "y": 64613.513640274046,
      "width": 473,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 944756939,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1176496299,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751044854,
      "created": 1790751042808,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "7. Another important problem: Data changing",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "7. Another important problem: Data changing",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "weqBnR0KMKXZAtqKOuTwY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -285.8114909022304,
      "y": 64655.513640274046,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 66657701,
      "version": 14,
      "versionNonce": 891818891,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751074553,
      "created": 1790751051561,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Imagine:\nPage 1\nProject A\nProject B\nProject C\n\nThen another user creates:\nProject X\n\nbefore you request page 2.\nWith certain offset-based approaches, records can shift between pages,\npotentially causing duplicates or missing records.\nCursor pagination can provide more stable traversal when the ordering is\ndesigned appropriately.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Imagine:\nPage 1\nProject A\nProject B\nProject C\n\nThen another user creates:\nProject X\n\nbefore you request page 2.\nWith certain offset-based approaches, records can shift between pages, potentially causing duplicates or missing records.\nCursor pagination can provide more stable traversal when the ordering is designed appropriately.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0KaG6Y2g_x_PFtCBTCj3f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -351.8114909022304,
      "y": 65069.513640274046,
      "width": 286,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 785980267,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1177857867,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751082185,
      "created": 1790751080384,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "8. Pagination vs Filtering",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "8. Pagination vs Filtering",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pt2qaI2b6LACnzQI_ZYzl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -302.9403971522304,
      "y": 65108.263640274046,
      "width": 473,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 477744389,
      "version": 27,
      "versionNonce": 1989529547,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751142157,
      "created": 1790751088752,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "These are different concepts.\nPagination\nAnswers:\nHow many records should I return?\n\nExample: /projects/?page=2\n\nFiltering\nAnswers:\nWhich records should I return?\n\nExample: /projects/?status=ACTIVE\n\nWe can combine them:\n/projects/?status=ACTIVE&page=2\n\nMeaning: Give me page 2 of active projects.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "These are different concepts.\nPagination\nAnswers:\nHow many records should I return?\n\nExample: /projects/?page=2\n\nFiltering\nAnswers:\nWhich records should I return?\n\nExample: /projects/?status=ACTIVE\n\nWe can combine them:\n/projects/?status=ACTIVE&page=2\n\nMeaning: Give me page 2 of active projects.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4rCZ2XEWbN5eAZFlFkbVJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -349.8114909022304,
      "y": 65611.51364027405,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 955596715,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1270365067,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751161184,
      "created": 1790751159885,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "9. Filtering in our Enterprise Workspace",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "9. Filtering in our Enterprise Workspace",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OMxy0im6of2mpsDIT8ADR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -306.4950846522304,
      "y": 65642.84957777405,
      "width": 748,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 667827397,
      "version": 35,
      "versionNonce": 496566091,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751229846,
      "created": 1790751167118,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Suppose Project has:\nProject\n├── name\n├── status\n├── team\n├── created_by\n└── created_at\n\nWe might support:\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE\nor\nGET /projects/?team=5\nor\nGET /projects/?created_by=10\nor\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE&team=5\n\nThe backend converts these query parameters into database filtering.\n\nConceptually\nprojects = Project.objects.filter(\n    status=\"ACTIVE\",\n    team_id=5\n)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Suppose Project has:\nProject\n├── name\n├── status\n├── team\n├── created_by\n└── created_at\n\nWe might support:\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE\nor\nGET /projects/?team=5\nor\nGET /projects/?created_by=10\nor\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE&team=5\n\nThe backend converts these query parameters into database filtering.\n\nConceptually\nprojects = Project.objects.filter(\n    status=\"ACTIVE\",\n    team_id=5\n)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kDGhIoH58OK3f9LQ0BWTa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -364.8114909022304,
      "y": 66324.01364027405,
      "width": 385,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1950129963,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 762432267,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751239621,
      "created": 1790751237417,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "10. Filtering + Searching + Sorting",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "10. Filtering + Searching + Sorting",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "y1EadLqiBbSkG1r_WJfhR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -333.5693034022304,
      "y": 66364.09957777405,
      "width": 781,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1305621829,
      "version": 47,
      "versionNonce": 1001557573,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751328317,
      "created": 1790751245920,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Production APIs often provide all three.\n\nFiltering\n/projects/?status=ACTIVE\nExact condition.\n\nSearching\n/projects/?search=payment\nFind projects matching \"payment\".\n\nSorting\n/projects/?ordering=-created_at\nNewest projects first.\n\n\nSo a realistic request might be:\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE&search=payment&ordering=-created_at&page=2\n\nMeaning\nActive projects\n      ↓\ncontaining \"payment\"\n      ↓\nnewest first\n      ↓\npage 2",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Production APIs often provide all three.\n\nFiltering\n/projects/?status=ACTIVE\nExact condition.\n\nSearching\n/projects/?search=payment\nFind projects matching \"payment\".\n\nSorting\n/projects/?ordering=-created_at\nNewest projects first.\n\n\nSo a realistic request might be:\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE&search=payment&ordering=-created_at&page=2\n\nMeaning\nActive projects\n      ↓\ncontaining \"payment\"\n      ↓\nnewest first\n      ↓\npage 2",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VhwIXHGRtlcdgvSXohOki",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -388.8114909022304,
      "y": 67099.51364027405,
      "width": 385,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1221662821,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1926649477,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751343521,
      "created": 1790751342104,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "11. One important backend principle",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "11. One important backend principle",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MtoUNvzva7GzFFG-8M-jY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -347.5458659022304,
      "y": 67143.90035902405,
      "width": 1080.84765625,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 609959979,
      "version": 103,
      "versionNonce": 1072774501,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790751378601,
      "created": 1790751349837,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Don't let the client filter on arbitrary database fields.\nBad:\n/projects/?some_secret_internal_field=...\nInstead, explicitly define which fields users are allowed to filter/search/order by.\nThis prevents accidental exposure of internal fields and keeps the API predictable.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Don't let the client filter on arbitrary database fields.\nBad:\n/projects/?some_secret_internal_field=...\nInstead, explicitly define which fields users are allowed to filter/search/order by.\nThis prevents accidental exposure of internal fields and keeps the API predictable.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yHo2wNWmLO7FeM3Y8BFP0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -407.7880534022304,
      "y": 67357.03707777405,
      "width": 737,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 586830955,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 1353880587,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262379123,
      "created": 1791262368185,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "if we are in 1st page and selected 20th page then what will happen?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "if we are in 1st page and selected 20th page then what will happen?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LnZi3ve9WSqkkAB0jWFvN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -377.9130534022304,
      "y": 67408.16207777405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1350516965,
      "version": 21,
      "versionNonce": 465943845,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262435763,
      "created": 1791262380851,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Limit/Offset pagination\nSuppose:\n- Total projects = 1,000,000\n- Page size = 20\n- User clicks page 20\nFrontend sends: GET /projects/?limit=20&offset=380\n\nBecause:\npage 1  → offset 0\npage 2  → offset 20\npage 3  → offset 40\n...\npage 20 → offset 380\n\nThe database conceptually does:\nSELECT *\nFROM projects\nORDER BY id\nLIMIT 20 OFFSET 380;\n\nSo it needs to account for the first 380 rows before returning the next\n20.\nFor page 20, that's perfectly reasonable.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Limit/Offset pagination\nSuppose:\n- Total projects = 1,000,000\n- Page size = 20\n- User clicks page 20\nFrontend sends: GET /projects/?limit=20&offset=380\n\nBecause:\npage 1  → offset 0\npage 2  → offset 20\npage 3  → offset 40\n...\npage 20 → offset 380\n\nThe database conceptually does:\nSELECT *\nFROM projects\nORDER BY id\nLIMIT 20 OFFSET 380;\n\nSo it needs to account for the first 380 rows before returning the next 20.\nFor page 20, that's perfectly reasonable.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "puc85pndbH2YUxKHAjyBa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -381.6630534022304,
      "y": 68031.66207777405,
      "width": 286,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1890919659,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1359685835,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262444096,
      "created": 1791262441517,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. What about page 45,000?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. What about page 45,000?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "BcAXEelhRrrf1VYLi9a5H",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -363.6669596522304,
      "y": 68061.78317152405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6c",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1865431941,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 2132264555,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262471667,
      "created": 1791262448862,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "offset = (45000 - 1) × 20\n       = 899,980\n\nThe query becomes roughly: LIMIT 20 OFFSET 899980\nNow the database may have to process/skip a very large number of rows,\nwhich can become expensive.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "offset = (45000 - 1) × 20\n       = 899,980\n\nThe query becomes roughly: LIMIT 20 OFFSET 899980\nNow the database may have to process/skip a very large number of rows, which can become expensive.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7F1CO0QtaXoyjErwM4unk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -387.6630534022304,
      "y": 68253.28317152405,
      "width": 363,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 473392011,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 174746475,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262480094,
      "created": 1791262478566,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Cursor pagination is different",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Cursor pagination is different",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FaLJFAprCw0oL9AWBl3d2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -359.6669596522304,
      "y": 68284.15817152405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6e",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1853009637,
      "version": 26,
      "versionNonce": 2139977253,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262545897,
      "created": 1791262484832,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Go directly to page 20\"\n\nInstead:\nPage 1\n   ↓ next cursor\nPage 2\n   ↓ next cursor\nPage 3\n   ↓ next cursor\n...\n\nThe cursor says approximately:\n\"Continue after this position.\"\n\nSo cursor pagination is excellent for things like:\nInfinite scrolling\nFeeds\nActivity logs\nHuge datasets\n\n\nBut numbered pages where the user can jump directly to page 20 are more\nnaturally implemented with offset/page-number pagination.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Go directly to page 20\"\n\nInstead:\nPage 1\n   ↓ next cursor\nPage 2\n   ↓ next cursor\nPage 3\n   ↓ next cursor\n...\n\nThe cursor says approximately:\n\"Continue after this position.\"\n\nSo cursor pagination is excellent for things like:\nInfinite scrolling\nFeeds\nActivity logs\nHuge datasets\n\n\nBut numbered pages where the user can jump directly to page 20 are more naturally implemented with offset/page-number pagination.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "khrry9LD2-eJgLoyCF4-m",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -422.6630534022304,
      "y": 68899.28317152405,
      "width": 275,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6f",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 270699589,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 706336357,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262553260,
      "created": 1791262551183,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Important interview point",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Important interview point",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "v2P41aVvLNP2L3fVdUVqd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -371.6630534022304,
      "y": 68931.28317152405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1227684837,
      "version": 7,
      "versionNonce": 1910432325,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262565600,
      "created": 1791262558199,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Don't say:\n\"Cursor pagination is always faster.\"\n\nInstead:\nOffset pagination is convenient for numbered pages, while cursor\npagination is generally better for deep pagination and continuously\nchanging large datasets, provided the ordering/cursor fields are indexed\nappropriately.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Don't say:\n\"Cursor pagination is always faster.\"\n\nInstead:\nOffset pagination is convenient for numbered pages, while cursor pagination is generally better for deep pagination and continuously changing large datasets, provided the ordering/cursor fields are indexed appropriately.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iivwu9DXjz_r43Phg0bxP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -446.5419596522304,
      "y": 69217.40426527405,
      "width": 781,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 518909029,
      "version": 7,
      "versionNonce": 1746466827,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262601218,
      "created": 1791262584366,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now back to our exercise:\n1,000,000 projects, frontend displays 20 at a time. What should we use?\nA) Return all 1,000,000 and let frontend split\nB) Backend pagination\nC) Store all projects permanently in Redis\nD) Send all projects through Celery",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now back to our exercise:\n1,000,000 projects, frontend displays 20 at a time. What should we use?\nA) Return all 1,000,000 and let frontend split\nB) Backend pagination\nC) Store all projects permanently in Redis\nD) Send all projects through Celery",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wiAG3iNsE_3jUJXXu0iJd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -421.8388346522304,
      "y": 69386.03317152405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2106478571,
      "version": 30,
      "versionNonce": 176882309,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262729194,
      "created": 1791262665948,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ Correct — B) Backend pagination\nWhy?\nIf we have:\n1,000,000 projects\n        ↓\nFrontend wants 20\n        ↓\nBackend returns only 20\n\nFor example: GET /projects/?page=1&page_size=20\n\nResponse:\n{\n  \"count\": 1000000,\n  \"next\": \"...page=2\",\n  \"results\": [\n    \"...20 projects...\"\n  ]\n}\n\nThis is better because:\n- ❌ Don't transfer 1M records over the network\n- ❌ Don't load 1M records into frontend memory\n- ❌ Don't make the API response huge\n- ✅ Database returns only the required data\n- ✅ Faster response\n- ✅ Lower memory/network usage\n\nInterview answer\nPagination should generally be handled by the backend so that the API\nreturns only the required subset of records instead of sending the\nentire dataset to the client.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ Correct — B) Backend pagination\nWhy?\nIf we have:\n1,000,000 projects\n        ↓\nFrontend wants 20\n        ↓\nBackend returns only 20\n\nFor example: GET /projects/?page=1&page_size=20\n\nResponse:\n{\n  \"count\": 1000000,\n  \"next\": \"...page=2\",\n  \"results\": [\n    \"...20 projects...\"\n  ]\n}\n\nThis is better because:\n- ❌ Don't transfer 1M records over the network\n- ❌ Don't load 1M records into frontend memory\n- ❌ Don't make the API response huge\n- ✅ Database returns only the required data\n- ✅ Faster response\n- ✅ Lower memory/network usage\n\nInterview answer\nPagination should generally be handled by the backend so that the API returns only the required subset of records instead of sending the entire dataset to the client.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JvPLxjDQsUPEknBRTsmIP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -504.6630534022304,
      "y": 70241.28317152405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1790112933,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1415224005,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262820708,
      "created": 1791262819378,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "so before next question previous answer doubt, in pagination frontend\nhits api everytime for the next response right?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "so before next question previous answer doubt, in pagination frontend hits api everytime for the next response right?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "otK8QFwlItvaq2S-fgoDa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -457.5419596522304,
      "y": 70308.02926527405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 1275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1414232043,
      "version": 30,
      "versionNonce": 1530205995,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791262890058,
      "created": 1791262825646,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Yes. ✅ In normal backend pagination, the frontend makes another API\nrequest whenever it needs another page.\nFor example, page size = 20:\n\nFrontend\n   │\n   │ GET /projects?page=1\n   ↓\nBackend\n   │\n   └── returns projects 1–20\n\nFrontend\n   │\n   │ GET /projects?page=2\n   ↓\nBackend\n   │\n   └── returns projects 21–40\n\nFrontend\n   │\n   │ GET /projects?page=3\n   ↓\nBackend\n   │\n   └── returns projects 41–60\n\nSo if the user clicks page 20, the frontend directly makes another API\ncall: GET /projects?page=20&page_size=20\n\nThe backend/database retrieves that page and sends it back.\nOne important point\nThe frontend doesn't necessarily call the API every time you move back\nto a page.\nFor example, the frontend could cache page 1:\n\nPage 1 → API call → store in frontend memory/cache\nPage 2 → API call → store\nPage 3 → API call → store\n\nBack to Page 1\n      ↓\nUse cached Page 1\n      ↓\nNo API call\n\nBut without frontend caching, yes:\nEvery new page requested = another API request.\nAnd this is actually one of the main benefits of pagination: you're\ntransferring only the data the user currently needs.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Yes. ✅ In normal backend pagination, the frontend makes another API request whenever it needs another page.\nFor example, page size = 20:\n\nFrontend\n   │\n   │ GET /projects?page=1\n   ↓\nBackend\n   │\n   └── returns projects 1–20\n\nFrontend\n   │\n   │ GET /projects?page=2\n   ↓\nBackend\n   │\n   └── returns projects 21–40\n\nFrontend\n   │\n   │ GET /projects?page=3\n   ↓\nBackend\n   │\n   └── returns projects 41–60\n\nSo if the user clicks page 20, the frontend directly makes another API call: GET /projects?page=20&page_size=20\n\nThe backend/database retrieves that page and sends it back.\nOne important point\nThe frontend doesn't necessarily call the API every time you move back to a page.\nFor example, the frontend could cache page 1:\n\nPage 1 → API call → store in frontend memory/cache\nPage 2 → API call → store\nPage 3 → API call → store\n\nBack to Page 1\n      ↓\nUse cached Page 1\n      ↓\nNo API call\n\nBut without frontend caching, yes:\nEvery new page requested = another API request.\nAnd this is actually one of the main benefits of pagination: you're transferring only the data the user currently needs.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "REXA3r4k4b-4S3c2NTQQB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -522.6630534022304,
      "y": 71659.28317152405,
      "width": 704,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2090681099,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1204976363,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791263003197,
      "created": 1791263001886,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Next Question — Filtering\nSuppose our Enterprise Workspace has 1,000,000 projects.\nThe user wants:\n\"Show me only ACTIVE projects.\"\n\nWhat should we do?\nA) Fetch all 1,000,000 projects and filter them in the frontend.\nB) Send the filter to the backend:\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE\n\nand let the database filter the projects.\nC) Fetch all projects into Redis first and filter there.\nD) Use Celery to filter the projects.\n👉 Choose A, B, C, or D.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Next Question — Filtering\nSuppose our Enterprise Workspace has 1,000,000 projects.\nThe user wants:\n\"Show me only ACTIVE projects.\"\n\nWhat should we do?\nA) Fetch all 1,000,000 projects and filter them in the frontend.\nB) Send the filter to the backend:\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE\n\nand let the database filter the projects.\nC) Fetch all projects into Redis first and filter there.\nD) Use Celery to filter the projects.\n👉 Choose A, B, C, or D.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ubt7Bf818Gxs-kolCKnm8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -470.9325846522304,
      "y": 72024.17379652405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 1575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 23078757,
      "version": 61,
      "versionNonce": 1108580165,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791263133070,
      "created": 1791263009552,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ Correct — B\nThe frontend sends the filter: GET /projects/?status=ACTIVE\n\nThen the flow is:\nFrontend\n   ↓\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE\n   ↓\nDjango API\n   ↓\nQueryset\n   ↓\nPostgreSQL\n   ↓\nOnly ACTIVE projects\n   ↓\nResponse\n\nFor example, Django might conceptually do:\n\nProject.objects.filter(status=\"ACTIVE\")\n\nWhy filter in the backend/database?\nSuppose there are:\n1,000,000 projects\n100,000 ACTIVE\n900,000 INACTIVE\n\nWe don't want to send all 1M projects to the frontend just so JavaScript\ncan throw away 900K.\n\nInstead:\nDatabase\n1M projects\n    ↓ filter\n100K ACTIVE\n    ↓ pagination\n20 projects\n    ↓\nFrontend\n\nImportant: Filtering + Pagination work together\nA real API might be:\n\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE&page=2&page_size=20\n\nThe meaning is:\n\"Give me the second page, 20 projects per page, but only among ACTIVE\nprojects.\"\n\nSo conceptually:\n\n1,000,000 projects\n        ↓\n   status = ACTIVE\n        ↓\n100,000 projects\n        ↓\n    pagination\n        ↓\n     20 projects\n\nThis is a very common backend pattern.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ Correct — B\nThe frontend sends the filter: GET /projects/?status=ACTIVE\n\nThen the flow is:\nFrontend\n   ↓\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE\n   ↓\nDjango API\n   ↓\nQueryset\n   ↓\nPostgreSQL\n   ↓\nOnly ACTIVE projects\n   ↓\nResponse\n\nFor example, Django might conceptually do:\n\nProject.objects.filter(status=\"ACTIVE\")\n\nWhy filter in the backend/database?\nSuppose there are:\n1,000,000 projects\n100,000 ACTIVE\n900,000 INACTIVE\n\nWe don't want to send all 1M projects to the frontend just so JavaScript can throw away 900K.\n\nInstead:\nDatabase\n1M projects\n    ↓ filter\n100K ACTIVE\n    ↓ pagination\n20 projects\n    ↓\nFrontend\n\nImportant: Filtering + Pagination work together\nA real API might be:\n\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE&page=2&page_size=20\n\nThe meaning is:\n\"Give me the second page, 20 projects per page, but only among ACTIVE projects.\"\n\nSo conceptually:\n\n1,000,000 projects\n        ↓\n   status = ACTIVE\n        ↓\n100,000 projects\n        ↓\n    pagination\n        ↓\n     20 projects\n\nThis is a very common backend pattern.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FKWOv9iRU9QcwDld6nEDq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -535.6630534022304,
      "y": 73685.17379652405,
      "width": 550,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6n",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1745011045,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 2031918981,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791263170629,
      "created": 1791263169285,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Next Question — Searching\nNow suppose the user types:\n\"payment\"\n\nThey want projects whose name contains \"payment\".\nWhich is better?\nA) Fetch all projects and search in frontend\nB) Send the search term to backend:\nGET /projects/?search=payment\n\nand let the database perform the search\nC) Use Celery to search all projects\nD) Store every project in Redis just for searching\n👉 Your answer?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Next Question — Searching\nNow suppose the user types:\n\"payment\"\n\nThey want projects whose name contains \"payment\".\nWhich is better?\nA) Fetch all projects and search in frontend\nB) Send the search term to backend:\nGET /projects/?search=payment\n\nand let the database perform the search\nC) Use Celery to search all projects\nD) Store every project in Redis just for searching\n👉 Your answer?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_5ZBzJcPyq_4XPMx8n10j",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -466.5771159022304,
      "y": 74064.86520277405,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 1075,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 309474565,
      "version": 43,
      "versionNonce": 1818212965,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791263378570,
      "created": 1791263275236,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ Correct — B\nFrontend sends:\n\nGET /projects/?search=payment\nBackend translates this into a database query, conceptually:\n\nProject.objects.filter(name__icontains=\"payment\")\n\nSo instead of:\n1,000,000 projects\n       ↓\nFrontend\n       ↓\nSearch \"payment\"\n\nwe do:\n1,000,000 projects\n       ↓\nPostgreSQL searches\n       ↓\nmatching projects\n       ↓\npagination\n       ↓\n20 results\n       ↓\nFrontend\n\nOne important distinction\nWe now have three concepts:\n\n| Feature | Purpose | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Pagination** | How many records? | `page=2&page_size=20` |\n| **Filtering** | Which category? | `status=ACTIVE` |\n| **Searching** | Find by text | `search=payment` |\n\nThey can be combined:\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE&search=payment&page=2&page_size=20\n\nMeaning:\nFind ACTIVE projects containing \"payment\", then give me page 2 with 20\nresults.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ Correct — B\nFrontend sends:\n\nGET /projects/?search=payment\nBackend translates this into a database query, conceptually:\n\nProject.objects.filter(name__icontains=\"payment\")\n\nSo instead of:\n1,000,000 projects\n       ↓\nFrontend\n       ↓\nSearch \"payment\"\n\nwe do:\n1,000,000 projects\n       ↓\nPostgreSQL searches\n       ↓\nmatching projects\n       ↓\npagination\n       ↓\n20 results\n       ↓\nFrontend\n\nOne important distinction\nWe now have three concepts:\n\n| Feature | Purpose | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Pagination** | How many records? | `page=2&page_size=20` |\n| **Filtering** | Which category? | `status=ACTIVE` |\n| **Searching** | Find by text | `search=payment` |\n\nThey can be combined:\nGET /projects/?status=ACTIVE&search=payment&page=2&page_size=20\n\nMeaning:\nFind ACTIVE projects containing \"payment\", then give me page 2 with 20 results.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "19WdLMvZWxqxxJdTd7LkB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -260.6630534022304,
      "y": 74080.17379652405,
      "width": 11,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
